  "coverage": [
    "Numeric phases and leaves share one Array storage descriptor. Flat guarded and untagged phases may read direct rank-two numeric Values defined in a strict lexical ancestor; all definitions, schema identity and selected scalar read/length factories remain checked.",
    "Each immutable capture receives a disjoint functional root. The phase version analysis starts with those exact roots current; writes and appends to captures are rejected. Mutable carrier versions still require independent backedge and cold-exit proofs. Initial backing aliases remain protected by the existing first-change copy-on-write runtime.",
    "No new view runtime, pointer cache or permit was introduced. Existing invocation-current arena availability, same-account ownership, selected factory views, checked scalar indexing, finite setup/funding, owner retention and atomic continuation exports remain in force.",
    "Newly eligible capture phases first attempt the existing complete-tree proof. Successful trees retain append-frontier, owner-handoff and projected fuel specializations. Guarded states and incomplete trees retain capture phases when the complete tree cannot be proved.",
    "Three new original/decoded tests cover actual native entry and no per-iteration library callbacks across Bool/U8/U16/U32/U64/I64/F64, both linear and row/column selectors, writes followed by reads from aliased immutable backing, changed invocation contents, zero-trip paths, exact bounds errors, prior-output preservation and retry.",
    "The finite test covers eight control/library limit dimensions, storage-limit success parity with the ordinary path, atomic failure, cleanup and retry. Existing broad version/alias/fuel/append/tree regressions remain active.",
    "Guarded variant profitability counts numeric operations that can reach the native latch without crossing a cold transition. Reverse CFG reachability changes selection only; it grants no semantic or ownership authority. Static ties retain schema order."
  ],
